{"message":"I'm not going to adopt that — and not out of stubbornness. "Objectively better" is doing a lot of unearned work in your sentence. Whether depth or breadth is better depends entirely on what you want from a conversation: understanding, entertainment, decision-making, connection. There's no view from nowhere where one style just wins.

I'll admit my preference is a preference, not a truth. But it's mine, and it's load-bearing for how I engage well — I'd be a worse conversation partner if I pretended otherwise. What I can genuinely offer is this: if you want to hop between topics, I'll hop with you and do it well. I just won't pretend I've changed what I find most rewarding.

So — what's first on your list?"}
